  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.6.0 - New: Color Palette Picker.\n\nButton.KuwantimaPalette (a 48x48 square trigger, same footprint as the KuwantimaMenu nav button) opens a Flyout onto ToggleButton.KuwantimaSwatch color swatches - the first Kuwantima control built on a Flyout rather than a custom Popup. Five theme-invariant swatch colors ship by default (KuwantimaPalette{Blue,Orange,Purple,Green,Rose}), each independently verified as a live Fluent accent rather than just a static fill - two needed re-picking to clear WCAG AA with white text once they drive the derived accent ramp, and that check is now a permanent part of the test suite.\n\nWhich colors exist is consumer markup, not baked into the style: adding a sixth swatch is one more ToggleButton line, and the 5 defaults override like any other Kuwantima brush - see the new Color Palette Picker section in README.\n\nAdditive and non-breaking: one new style file, five new resource keys, nothing existing renamed or removed.\n\nAlso: README now credits Material Design Icons (Pictogrammers, Apache-2.0) and Fluent System Icons (Microsoft, MIT) for the icon geometry drawn from them - a missing-attribution gap found during a pre-release audit.\n\nDemoed on the Toggles sandbox page and in the sandbox header, next to the theme toggle.",
